<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malaysian Chinese Association</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949–</span> · Also known as Malayan Chinese Association, MCA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Malaysian Chinese Association, founded in 1949 as the Malayan Chinese Association under Tan Cheng Lock, is a political party representing ethnic Chinese in Malaysia. It began partly as a welfare body for Chinese moved into new villages during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malayan-emergency">Malayan Emergency</a>. It joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-malays-national-organisation">United Malays National Organisation</a> in the Alliance that won independence in 1957 and remained a partner in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-nasional">Barisan Nasional</a> coalition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malaysian-chinese-association.jpg" alt="Malaysian Chinese Association" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Great Brightstar (originally Malaysian Chinese Association) · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_Malaysian_Chinese_Association.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
